<!--
  RM_Bitumen.xml                       TheSump (moved from UtinniPatches by SUMP_FREE_TIER_MOVE_BUILD_1) — SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1

  Item spec §4, "the tar's own reward — annoying materials pay: the sheet
  already calls the tar biologically rich; pick the reward with the roster
  docs." the_sump.md §7 already names the axis directly: "Bitumen —
  waterproofing, adhesive, torch-fuel, and asphalt: the Ashfall Road's
  material now has its source." sump_flora_roster_2026-09-24.md row 4
  (`RM_Korveth`) independently confirms the same def as ITS OWN harvest
  ("the bitumen accumulator... harvest yields a bitumen item — shared item
  def with the dig economy... 🆕 NEW def only — the item; no C#") and marks
  it **OWED**. So this is not an invented reward: it is a def two separate
  design passes already asked for and neither had shipped.

  Fuel/chemistry axis (not preservation — that is SUMP_TAR_VAULT_1's own
  rot-stop mechanism, a different item, kept distinct rather than doubled
  up on the same material).

  🔑 A genuine correction, same pass this item was authored: SUMP_WALKWAYS_1
  flagged RM_Glasswalk's own costList (Chemfuel x6) as "PLACEHOLDER... OWED:
  re-point at the real bitumen/dig-barrel chain... once the items pass ships
  it" — that items pass is this def, so RM_SumpWalkways.xml is repointed to
  RM_Bitumen in this same commit (CLAUDE.md: "correctness outranks seat
  ownership" applies even to one's own prior-session placeholder).

  The source: the roster's own
  korveth plant now ships (RM_Korveth); this def renders from its harvest,
  RM_KorvethPitch, at a machining table (2 : 1, WorkToMake 200), the recipe
  that used to ride UtinniPatches' RUT_Bitumen_KorvethSource.xml, inlined
  here by SUMP_FREE_TIER_MOVE_BUILD_1. RM_Glasswalk spends it.
  "Make gathering it want the coping gear" (item spec §4's own closing
  line): a future korveth-harvest or dig-barrel job hauling raw bitumen out
  of tar country is the natural place to risk tarring the harvester
  (RM_Filth_Tar/RM_Tarred) without a weak solvent on hand — flagged as a
  design note for whichever pass builds that job, not implemented here
  (no harvest job exists yet to attach the risk to).

  Texture: a first draft reused vanilla Things/Item/Resource/Jade as a
  placeholder, same choice RM_ThrummelSeepwax made — but validate_patch.py
  refuses that as a hard ERROR for the same reason documented on that def's
  own file (UtinniPatches already claims Textures/Things/Item/Resource/ as
  its own namespace). Repointed to a new RM_Bitumen/ folder (Graphic_
  StackCount reads texPath as a folder, same Graphic_Collection finding)
  with a simple procedurally-drawn placeholder chunk icon, near-black with
  a slight sheen — distinct from RM_ThrummelSeepwax's warm amber so the
  two are never visually confused on a shelf.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RM_Bitumen</defName>
    <label>bitumen</label>
    <description>Solid black pitch, rendered from raw tar until it sets hard. Waterproofing, adhesive, torch-fuel, road-metal — half the Sump's economy runs on this one substance in one form or another, and the old paved roads were made from exactly this.</description>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RM_Bitumen</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <color>(24, 22, 20)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>1.8</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.35</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.7</Flammability>
      <WorkToMake>200</WorkToMake>
      <DeteriorationRate>1</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <stackLimit>100</stackLimit>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
    <recipeMaker>
      <recipeUsers>
        <li>TableMachining</li>
      </recipeUsers>
      <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
      <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
      <displayPriority>425</displayPriority>
      <productCount>1</productCount>
    </recipeMaker>
    <costList>
      <RM_KorvethPitch>2</RM_KorvethPitch>
    </costList>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
